# Normalise line endings in the repository regardless of the committer's core.autocrlf.
#
# Every tracked file here is text -- ts, vue, css, json, yml, mjs, md -- and every committed blob
# is already LF. The working tree is what drifts: with core.autocrlf=true on Windows, git checks
# these out as CRLF, so the same file is two different byte streams on two machines while the
# repository holds one. A consumer comparing files across sibling repos then sees a difference
# that exists in neither of them.
#
# Same rule the sibling repos already carry, so `* text=auto eol=lf` is the convention rather than
# a third answer. Reported by a consumer who hit exactly this on LICENSE.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never touch, never diff as text. Nothing binary is committed today -- this is the safety
# net for the first font, icon or screenshot that arrives, since the rule above would otherwise
# treat a file git guessed wrong about as text and corrupt it on checkout.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.pdf binary
